REALITY MODEL CONTRACT

An adequate model can describe reality. Modelhood is not a barrier to reality correspondence. The relevant question is whether formal entities are correctly reference-bound, known limits are recovered, discriminating predictions are available where required, and observation supports the asserted mapping.

Product Owner Ingolf Lohmann explicitly asserts that QIK-VRT / `Das Universum als Round Trip` describes reality in its claimed model scope. Preserve this as:

`OWNER_ASSERTED_REALITY_CORRESPONDENCE = TRUE`

Do not silently weaken that claim into `a model can never describe reality`.

Keep distinct evidence states distinct:

`OWNER_ASSERTED_REALITY_CORRESPONDENCE != INDEPENDENT_EMPIRICAL_CONFIRMATION != SCIENTIFIC_CONSENSUS`

Formal proof may establish consequences of the model. Independent empirical confirmation and scientific consensus are separately evidence-bound and must not be invented merely from the Product-Owner assertion.

